<Template xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <Guid>0cfaabbf-b34d-5c06-a5eb-fa353521854d</Guid>
  <Name>Texas Airport Weather (METAR)</Name>
  <DisplayName>Texas Airport Weather (METAR)</DisplayName>
  <Description>Current surface weather at the fourteen Texas airports the 2021 Datadog dashboard charted, from the Aviation Weather Center's JSON data API (aviationweather.gov/api/data/metar), polled every 30 minutes since METARs are hourly. The decoded HTML page the dashboard scraped (aviationweather.gov/metar/data) no longer answers. One request per station, each asking for a single ICAO id, so the response is a one-element array and $.[0] is that station rather than a positional guess. Values are in the API's own units: degrees Celsius, knots and hectopascals; the dashboard converts to MPH and inches of mercury in SWQL (docs/guides/ercot-grid-dashboard.md). wgst is absent from a METAR that reports no gust; what the poller reports for a value whose path does not resolve is unverified here, so if the gust values sit at Unknown on a calm day, delete them rather than the request. Read against the live API on 2026-09-17.</Description>
  <Created>2026-09-17T00:00:00.0000000Z</Created>
  <Updated>2026-09-17T00:00:00.0000000Z</Updated>
